  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_014: multimodal, scgpt+imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted → acc 0.52), the most critical uncertainty is whether the multimodal fusion is actually contributing positively or is adding noise. Config_015 (image_only, multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, transformer) is a clean ablation of config_014: it removes the RNA modality while keeping the same image encoder, aggregation, and profile setting. If image-only achieves comparable or better accuracy, the RNA branch is not helping and the remaining 8 experiments should focus on image-only or alternative RNA encoders. If image-only is substantially worse, multimodal fusion is confirmed as beneficial and we can exploit that direction. This single experiment resolves a high-impact design question early, preventing us from wasting budget optimizing a potentially unhelpful component."
}

